Accordingly, I pass the following:
Dhanasekaran vs Arfath A on 15 April, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/161994585/
4 ORDER i) The appeal is allowed-in-part;
ii) The judgment and award dated 07.01.2022 passed in MVC.No.2471/2019 by XXII Additional Small Causes and Additional MACT, Bengaluru, is modified;
iii) The claimant is entitled to a total compensation of Rs.5,84,400/- as against Rs.3,92,000/- awarded by the tribunal with interest @ 6% p.a.;
iv) The enhanced compensation amount shall be paid with interest @ 6% p.a. within a period - 10 - NC: 2024:KHC:14953 of four weeks from the date of receipt of a copy of this judgment;
v) The compensation amount shall be released in favour of the appellant-claimant upon proper verification;
vi) All other terms and conditions stipulated by the tribunal shall stand intact.
